.SH NAME
lmm-update-rollback - Rollback a mod to its previous version


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBlmm update rollback <mod-id> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Rollback a mod to the version before the last update.

.PP
The previous version must still be available in the cache. If the same
mod ID is installed from more than one source in the profile, use
-s/--source to disambiguate.

.PP
--json prints the single-mod document (see 'lmm update --help') with
status "rolled_back", or status "skipped" with reason "locked" when the
mod is locked (unlock or move the lock to roll back).

.PP
Examples:
  lmm update rollback 12345 --game skyrim-se
  lmm update rollback 12345 --game skyrim-se --source nexusmods


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-f\fP, \fB--force\fP[=false]
	continue even if hooks fail

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for rollback

.PP
\fB-p\fP, \fB--profile\fP=""
	profile (default: active profile)

.PP
\fB-s\fP, \fB--source\fP=""
	mod source (default: the sole configured source; prompts when several are configured)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	config directory (default: ~/.config/lmm)

.PP
\fB--data\fP=""
	data directory (default: ~/.local/share/lmm)

.PP
\fB-g\fP, \fB--game\fP=""
	game ID to operate on

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	output in JSON format (list, status, search, update, conflicts, verify, mod show, source list)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	disable colored output (NO_COLOR env is also honored)

.PP
\fB--no-hooks\fP[=false]
	disable all hooks

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	verbose output


